A||||34||87ECO5||Ohio Fieros Icebreaker Cookout||||1||
Z||000000||87ECO5||02-23-2000||10:07 AM||||I'm at it again.  What do you all think about getting together for the first big cookout of the year?  Sort of a way to celebrate the arrival of Spring (do we really NEED a reason to celebrate!?).<P>Anyway, I've got some dates and locations to run by all of you.  Let me know what you think.<P>Dates - Since Spring officially arrives on (I believe) March 21st, I thought Saturday, the 25th would be appropriate with a rain date of the following weekend, Saturday, April 1st.<P>Locations - I thought of two places.  First one is Hueston Woods.  Beautiful area, pretty easy to get to, close for the Indiana folks.  Second one is Caesar's Creek Gorge.  Beautiful area, easy to get to, close for the Columbus folks.  I don't have much info on Hueston Woods right now.  I was out at the gorge last weekend and they've installed a new shelter and grill pits.<P>Dates - No, not dates as in March or April.  Dates as in husbands, wives, boyfriends girlfriends, etc.  I thought it'd be nice to bring the significant others along.  I don't have to remind anyone how beneficial this would be.<P>So, let me know what you think.  More details to follow ...||||reg||1
Z||000001||william_thorniii||02-23-2000||12:47 PM||||87EC05,<P>Again not a solid commitment from me, but it does sound fun.  I have beat you to the first BBQ of the year though.  I cooked out last night.  Of course BBQ with me is not a seasonal thing, it only thins out in the winter.  <P>The way I figure, you are going to have to get another Fiero soon.  If you are going to bring 3 dates that is.  I am sure that Rachael and Meagan would love to join in on this fun.  But it would be down right blasphemy to arrive in the Pathfinder.  So I figure you get Lisa a Fiero then you can load the passenger seats with car seats and you will truly be a Fiero-family.  <P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000002||BOILERMAKER||02-23-2000||12:53 PM||||I am definitely interested in this function.  I will be unable to attend this upcoming function due to some issues that can't be helped, but the next function should be just fine with me.  You name the place and I'll bring some food (well, I'd probably have to buy some closer to where the function is).||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||02-23-2000||01:28 PM||||If I find a nice apartment, I'll be moving on one of those two weekends.  So I will most likely have to pass.<P>Of course, if I find a nicer apartment that doesn't have scumbag neighbors, that means I can own two Fieros again and leave one at home all day without some SOB egging it!  Happy happy joy joy!||||reg||9
Z||000004||87ECO5||02-24-2000||07:34 AM||||<B>william_thorniii</B> - unless you had a bunch of Fiero nuts over, you haven't beat me to it!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   Unfortunately (or fortunately    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   ), I won't be bringing Roo and Moo to this one, so a single Fiero will suffice (although you've got one heck of an argument for me to use on Lisa!).<P><B>BOILERMAKER</B> - glad to hear you're interested.  I hope your dad's surgery goes well today.<P><B>ChadMan</B> - I'm not putting you down as 'no' just yet, pal!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||87ECO5||02-28-2000||12:40 PM||||Just posting a list of attendees so far:<P><B>87ECO5</B> and my wife, <B><I>Lisa</I></B><BR><B>fiero56</B> (probably)<BR><B>william_thorniii</B> (maybe)<BR><B>BENGAL4</B> and his wife, <B><I>Stormy</I></B> (maybe)<BR><B>BOILERMAKER</B> (probably)<P>Wow, this might turn into an 87ECO5 family thing.  Seriously though, I'm not set on the suggested dates or locations.  That's just it - they're only suggestions.  If it's better to move the date up or back, or have it somewhere else, I'm very much open to alternatives.  Heck, we could have it at my place this weekend, but you'd all have to help me put a starter on the coupe between burgers!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Let me know, folks ...||||reg||1
