Z||000013||87ECO5||03-07-2000||03:35 PM||||OK, here's the deal.<P>Lisa and I will be at Caesar's Creek Gorge on Saturday, April 1st at 11AM - weather permitting.  The grill pit will be hot shortly thereafter.<P>Now, what we need:<P>charcoal - 87ECO5<BR>burgers and dogs - 87ECO5<BR>buns -<BR>chips -<BR>potato or macaroni salad -<BR>junk food -<BR>condiments (cheese, mustard, ketchup, relish, etc.) - <BR>plates -<BR>utensils - 87ECO5<BR>cups -<BR><B>what have I missed?</B><P>These are the things I like but it's by no means a complete list.  Since I'm bringing the meat, make sure you let me know if you're coming so I can buy enough.  Oh, and it's BYOB (bring your own beverage).  For those on diets, if you'd rather have something other than beef, bring it - we'll get it cooked.<P>Festivities?  Well, I've got a frisbee and a hackysack.  Also, overflow from the lake goes right by the shelter.  So, if you're into it, bring a fishing rod.  And, of course, there's Fiero chat.<P>Rain date will be the following weekend, 4/8.<P>Questions/comments/concerns - contact me directly.||||reg||1
Z||000014||87ECO5||03-07-2000||08:56 PM||||Easy directions ... from I-71/SR73 interchange:<P>- Go West on SR73 for 7.9 miles.<BR>- Turn left onto Clarksville Road.<BR>- Go South on Clarksville Road for 2.5 miles.<BR>- Turn right onto access road.<BR>- Go 0.8 miles.  Road dead-ends into picnic shelter.<P>Total trip from I-71/SR73 interchange is about 13 minutes.<P>Now, for those coming the other direction ...<P>From downtown Springboro (SR741/SR73 interchange):<P>- Go East on SR73 for 9.9 miles.<BR>- Turn right onto Clarksville Road.<BR>- (from here, follow above instructions).<P>Total trip from SR741/SR73 interchange is about 18 minutes.<P><B>BOILERMAKER</B> - Not sure which route you're using to get to Dayton, but it might be easier for you to come 70 East to 75 South to SR73 ... fairly straight shot.<P>Hope this helps ...||||reg||1
